UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032229227?origin=resultslist
AD  - Laboratory of Geodynamics, Geophysical center of the Russian Academy of Sciences, 3, Molodezhnaya St, Moscow, 119296, Russian Federation
AD  - Department of Safety and Ecology in Mining of the Mining Institute, MISIS University of Science and Technology, Moscow, bld. 1, 4, Leninsky Ave., Moscow, 119049, Russian Federation
AB  - Introduction. The territory of the Republic of North Ossetia–Alania is characterized by intense geodynamic processes, which makes it necessary to identify neotectonic activation zones for natural hazard assessment. Purpose of the research. The aim of the study is to identify geodynamically active zones within the “Ossetian Geodynamic Polygon” using a set of geomorphic indices. Materials and methods. Morpholineament density, the mountain front sinuosity index (Smf), the normalized channel steepness index (Ksn), and knickpoint density were used. Sentinel-2B satellite imagery and the FABDEM digital elevation model served as the main datasets. Calculations were performed in MATLAB (TopoToolbox-2). Results. The highest morpholineament density occurs along the southern margin of the «Ossetian Depression», especially near the convergence of the Vladikavkaz and Ardon faults, and in the valleys of the Ardon and Terek rivers. A previously unmapped morpholineament was identified near Tarskoe. Smf values range from 1.12 to 1.27, and two mountain fronts are distinguished in the eastern part of the area. High Ksn values (400–500) and increased knickpoint density form a narrow linear zone between the Buron–Lars and Shaukhokh thrust faults. Discussion. Smf values confirm high tectonic activity; multiple fronts are typical of thrust systems. The low variability of Smf indicates approximately uniform uplift rates along the mountain front. Elevated Ksn values between the Buron–Lars and Shaukhokh thrusts likely reflect recent reactivation expressed by intensified river incision. Conclusion. The integrated use of geomorphological indices allowed identifying neotectonic activation zones within the “Ossetian Geodynamic Polygon”. Resume. Neotectonic activation zones consistent with major fault structures were identified. Smf values indicate high activity along the southern margin of the «Ossetian Depression» and uniform uplift rates. High Ksn values and knickpoint density form a linear zone between the Buron–Lars and Shaukhokh thrusts, reflecting recent tectonic activity. The results may support seismic zoning, mapping active fault zones, and assessing natural hazards. Further research should integrate geomorphological indices with GNSS monitoring to refine interpretations of the modern geodynamic regime. © 2025, North Caucasian Institute of Mining and Metallurgy, State Technological University. All rights reserved.
