TI  - COMPARISON OF THE COSEISMIC DEFORMATION FIELDS OF THE MADUO EARTHQUAKE OBSERVED BY DIFFERENT METHODS OF INSAR, OPTICAL IMAGING AND UAV, AND ITS CONSTRAINT ABILITY ON THE FAULT SLIP MODEL
PY  - 2025
T2  - International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium (IGARSS)  
SP  - 9506
EP  - 9509
DO  - 10.1109/IGARSS55030.2025.11242562
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105034105596?origin=resultslist
AD  - State Key Laboratory of Earthquake Dynamics, Institute of Geology, China Earthquake Administration, Beijing, China
AB  - The coseismic deformation field around the seismogenic fault, especially the distribution and change characteristics of near-field deformation, provides important constraints for the fine inversion of the slip distribution model. Here，we use Sentinel-1 satellite data to obtain the coseismic deformation field of the Maduo earthquake by InSAR and offset techniques，and quantitatively compare it with the results from optical imaging and UAV/field investigations. We inverted the coseismic slip models based on different observation data and four fault models. The results show that compared to InSAR, optical imaging and offset tracking can better reflect the near-fault deformation trend (<2 km). The relative displacement measured by both the InSAR and offset methods is larger than that measured in the field. The eastern branch fault model with GPS, InSAR and offset data is the optimal coseismic slip distribution model for Maduo earthquake, and the maximum slip is 5.55 m. ©2025 IEEE.
