AB  - Article title: YOLOv5-RF: a deep learning method for tailings pond identification in high-resolution remote sensing images based on improved loss function Authors: Weiming Zhang, Wenliang Jiang, Qiang Li, Yi Luo, Heng Zhang, Qisong Jiao, Yongsheng Li and Hongbo Jiang Journal: Big Earth DataDOI: https://doi.org/10.1080/20964471.2024.2436230 When the article was initially published online, Notes on contributors was typeset incorrectly. The error has since been corrected, and the updated version has been republished online.Incorrect: (Figure presented.) Qiang Li received the Ph.D. degree in disaster prevention and mitigation engineering from the Institute of Engineering Mechanics, China Earthquake Administration, in 2018. His research interests include remote sensing disaster information extraction and emergency assessment, multi-source remote sensing information analysis, and landslide hazard risk assessment. (Figure presented.) Yi Luo received the M.S. degree in geophysics from the Institute of Crustal Dynamics, China Earthquake Administration, in 2008. His research interests include distribution of earthquake deformation, modeling of crustal block motion, active fault movements, and InSAR/GNSS applications in those fields. (Figure presented.) Heng Zhang received the M.S. degree in mining engineering from University of Science and Technology Beijing, China, in 2015. His research interests include the development of intelligent mining systems and the application of three-dimensional mining planning software such as GEOVIA Surpac, Micromine, and 3Dmine, as well as three-dimensional blasting design software in mining engineering. (Figure presented.) Qisong Jiao received the Ph.D. degree in disaster prevention and mitigation engineering from the Institute of Engineering Mechanics, China Earthquake Administration, in 2015. His research interests include 3D reconstruction, LiDAR application and remote sensing of disaster.Corrected: (Figure presented.) Qiang Li received the Ph.D. degree in disaster prevention and mitigation engineering from the Institute of Engineering Mechanics, China Earthquake Administration, Beijing, China, in 2018. His research interests include remote sensing disaster information extraction and emergency assessment, multi-source remote sensing information analysis, and landslide hazard risk assessment. (Figure presented.) Yi Luo received the M.S. degree in geophysics from the Institute of Crustal Dynamics (ICD), China Earthquake Administration, Beijing, China, in 2008. His research interests include distribution of earthquake deformation, modeling of crustal block motion, active fault movements, and InSAR/GNSS applications in those fields. (Figure presented.) Heng Zhang received the M.S. degree in mining engineering from University of Science and Technology Beijing, Beijing, China, in 2015. His research interests include the development of intelligent mining systems and the application of three-dimensional mining planning software such as GEOVIA Surpac, Micromine, and 3Dmine, as well as three-dimensional blasting design software in mining engineering. (Figure presented.) Qisong Jiao received the Ph.D. degree in disaster prevention and mitigation engineering from the Institute of Engineering Mechanics, China Earthquake Administration, Beijing, China, in 2015. His research interests include 3D reconstruction, LiDAR application and remote sensing of disaster. © 2025 The Author(s). Published by Taylor & Francis Group and Science Press on behalf of the International Society for Digital Earth, supported by the International Research Center of Big Data for Sustainable Development Goals, and CASEarth Strategic Priority Research Programme.
